id: pm-89neyq
title: "Sentry PM-CLI-2N: malformed missing tags crash normalizeItemMetadata before search can report the item"
description: "Release 2026.7.28 emitted two handled high-severity search failures because normalizeItemMetadata assumes tags is always an array and calls tags.map before malformed legacy or extension-authored item metadata can be normalized or diagnosed. This is distinct from closed pm-d7us, which guarded the later search scorer tags.join path."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: bugfix,metadata,observability,regression,search,sentry
created_at: "2026-07-28T04:37:06.710Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T04:50:15.100Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T04:50:11.553Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A failing regression test proves absent tags no longer throw; canonical normalization emits an empty sorted tag array; search/read integration remains green; full coverage and release reliability gates pass; Sentry is resolved only after exact fix evidence.
parent: pm-rnpb
severity: high
environment: production
resolution: Canonical metadata normalization now treats absent/non-array runtime tags as an empty collection and filters malformed non-string legacy entries before trim/lowercase normalization; replay fallback coverage was moved to a genuinely uncanonicalizable legacy value.
expected_result: Search and all SDK read paths normalize absent tags safely without emitting a raw TypeError.
actual_result: "The exact failing regression now returns [] for absent tags and normalized string-only output for malformed arrays; focused, linked, full-coverage, static-quality, and type gates pass."
affected_version: 2026.7.28
fixed_version: unreleased
component: core/item-format
regression: true
